      texture: "Littleneck has a cross-hatched sculpture where radial ribs cross concentric growth lines; Manila has stronger radiating ribs.",
      size: "Roughly 3-6 cm; harvestable at 1.5 in (38 mm).",
      shell: "Thick equal valves; the inner ventral margin is finely crenulated (toothed) in the native littleneck.",
      keyFeatures: ["Cross-hatched (littleneck) or ribbed, mottled (Manila) sculpture", "Crenulated inner shell margin in littleneck", "Short fused siphons (split at the tips in Manila)", "Purple interior staining common in Manila"],
