    culinary: { flavor: "Sweet, mild, and briny; Manila clams are the standard PNW steamer clam", uses: "Steamed with wine/garlic, in pasta (vongole), chowder, and broths", preservation: "Best cooked fresh; freezing shucked meat is possible but does not reduce biotoxin risk" },
    conservationNotes: "Manila clams are introduced and support much of the recreational fishery; native littlenecks grow more slowly. Refill holes to protect other buried clams and juveniles, and observe minimum-size and daily limits.",
